points = dict(balance=170000, availableFrom='2026-10-15', notes='Update 13 Sep 2026: the flight home was booked as a paid Economy Sale fare, which cannot be upgraded with points (Sale classes E/N/O/Q are excluded from Classic Upgrade Rewards). Only the Jetstar feeder (5,700) has used points, so about 164k stay in the bank; Economy Plus on QF80 (~19,500 pts if offered) is the one remaining use on this trip. Prices confirmed post-5 Aug 2025: NRT→BNE Business 82,100; HND/NRT→SYD/MEL Business 98,400; short domestic (Zone 1) economy 9,200 + ~A$58. Economy Tokyo→Brisbane is estimated at ~29,000 (Zone 5) and Tokyo→Sydney/Melbourne ~36,200 (Zone 6); the exact cells were not visible from here, confirm on qantas.com. Bronze members are last in the upgrade queue and are typically only considered inside 24 h of departure, so treat any upgrade as a bonus, not a plan. Qantas’ Flight Reward Finder can be searched without logging in; AwardFares has a free Qantas search with alerts.')

