questions.insert(0, dict(id='q13', question='Kamakura or Yamaguchi: can either fit?', why='Kamakura (Great Buddha, Hase-dera, the Enoden tram along the coast) is an hour from Tokyo and a proper day. On this trip Tokyo is only a transit point: the morning you land (jet-lagged, heading to Osaka) and the afternoon you fly home (Takayama to Narita already takes the day). Fitting it means leaving Takayama a day early, forfeiting the prepaid Monday night, paying for a Tokyo hotel and moving the suitcase again, for about three hours in Kamakura with the airport clock running. Yamaguchi (Rurikoji pagoda, Akiyoshido cave, Motonosumi shrine, Hagi) is at the far western end of Honshu, two and a half hours beyond Osaka by Shinkansen and spread out enough to need a car; it is a two- or three-day region of its own, not a detour.', options=['Leave both for another trip (planned)', 'Kamakura on 16 Feb: leave Takayama on the 15th, sleep in Tokyo, 3 h in Kamakura before Narita', 'Yamaguchi: not possible without dropping Koyasan or the Takayama hub'], recommendation='Leave both. Kamakura is the first thing to do on a future Tokyo-based trip (spring or autumn, weekday). Yamaguchi pairs with Hiroshima and Miyajima on a western trip.', answer='Neither this trip. Kamakura first on the next Tokyo trip; Yamaguchi with Hiroshima on a western trip.', resolved=True))
questions.insert(0, dict(id='q12', question='Plan A (ski) or Plan B (no skiing)?', why='Both use the flights already booked and the same Osaka and USJ days; they split on Thursday 11 Feb. Plan A: Nozawa Onsen for five nights, three ski days plus a rural Sunday, hinges on finding a solo room in a sold-out week. Plan B: Takayama as a four-night hub (one room, unpack once), with two nights out in great places (a temple at Koyasan, a farmhouse at Shirakawa-go), free afternoons and a free day, and no start before 9:30 except USJ, which the Express Pass makes optional. No dependence on Nozawa, and about A$500 cheaper because there are no lifts or rental. Lost workdays are identical. The plan switch at the top of the menu flips every page between them.', options=['Plan A: ski trip (Nozawa Onsen)', 'Plan B: Takayama hub with Koyasan and Shirakawa-go nights out', 'Hybrid: Plan B with two of the Takayama nights swapped for Nozawa without skiing (onsen village, snow, food)'], recommendation='Decide by accommodation: if a Nozawa room lands by late October, Plan A. If not, Plan B is not a consolation prize; the Koyasan and Shirakawa-go nights are two of the best things you can do in Japan in winter, and every bed in it is easier to get.', answer='Plan B', resolved=True))

